              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "تماشاگر (tamâshâgar) — \"a spectator\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "تماشاگران تا آخر بازی ماندند. Tamâshâgarân tâ âkhar-e bâzi mândand. The spectators stayed until the end of the game."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "tamâshâ \"watching\" + -gar. Plural tamâshâgarân."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "tamâshâgar adds the Persian suffix -gar to tamâshâ \"watching, a show\", which EtymDB derives from the Arabic verb mashā \"to walk\", so first a stroll about, then a show."
            }
          ]
        },
